+ name: new-agent
+ description: Create a new OpenClaw agent with its own workspace and connect it to a messaging channel (Telegram, Discord, Slack, Feishu, WhatsApp, Signal, or Google Chat). Triggers on phrases like "create a new agent", "add a bot", "new team member", "onboard agent".
+ # New Agent
+ Create a new OpenClaw agent with its own workspace and bind it to a messaging channel.
+ Use this skill when the user wants to:
+ - Create a new AI agent or bot
+ - Add a new team member bot
+ - Connect a new bot to a messaging channel
+ Required information:
+ - `CHANNEL`: Channel type (telegram / discord / slack / feishu / whatsapp / signal / googlechat)
+ Read `/root/.openclaw/openclaw.json` and make these three changes:
+ ### b) Add channel account
+ #### 📱 Telegram
+ Credentials needed: Bot Token (from @BotFather)
+ > ⚠️ Token must go in `accounts.{name}.botToken`, not at top level.
+ #### 🎮 Discord
+ Credentials needed: Bot Token (from [Discord Developer Portal](https://discord.com/developers/applications))
+ Steps:
+ Steps:
+ Steps:
+ 1. New Application → Bot tab → Reset Token → copy token
+ 2. Enable **Message Content Intent** under Privileged Gateway Intents
+ 3. OAuth2 → URL Generator → scope `bot` → invite to server
+ #### 💬 Slack
+ Credentials needed: App Token (`xapp-...`) + Bot Token (`xoxb-...`)
+ 1. [api.slack.com/apps](https://api.slack.com/apps) → Create New App
+ 2. Enable **Socket Mode** → generate App Token with `connections:write` scope
+ 3. OAuth & Permissions → install app → copy Bot Token
+ #### 🪁 Feishu / Lark
+ Credentials needed: App ID + App Secret (from [Feishu Open Platform](https://open.feishu.cn/app))
+ 1. Create Enterprise App → copy App ID and App Secret
+ 2. Enable Bot capability
+ 3. Subscribe event: `im.message.receive_v1`
+ 4. Enable WebSocket event subscription
+ > For Lark (global), add `"domain": "lark"` to the config.
+ #### 💚 WhatsApp
